The {{nihongo|'''Daihatsu Thor'''|ダイハツ・トール|Daihatsu Tōru|lead=yes}} (also called {{nihongo|'''Toyota Roomy'''/'''Tank'''|トヨタ・ルーミー/トヨタ・タンク|Toyota Rūmī/Toyota Tanku|lead=yes}} and {{nihongo|'''Subaru Justy'''|スバル・ジャスティ|Subaru Jasuti|lead=yes}}) is a [[mini MPV]] with [[Sliding door (car)|sliding doors]]<!-- Not a kei car since its engine is 996 cc in displacement (a kei car must have a maximum engine displacement of 660 cc) --> designed and manufactured by [[Daihatsu]], and sold by Daihatsu, [[Toyota]] and [[Subaru]].<ref>{{cite news |url=http://topauto.site/tank-vs-thor-toyota-daihatsu-and-subaru-showed-a-family-of-mitrofanov/ |title=Tank vs Thor: Toyota, Daihatsu and Subaru showed a family of Mitrofanov |work=Top Auto |date=2017-02-23 |access-date=2017-04-15 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170517014029/http://topauto.site/tank-vs-thor-toyota-daihatsu-and-subaru-showed-a-family-of-mitrofanov/ |archive-date=17 May 2017 |url-status=dead }}</ref> It is a five-seat MPV based on the [[Daihatsu Boon#M700|M700 series Boon]] and was introduced on 9 November 2016<ref>{{cite news |url=http://techon.nikkeibp.co.jp/atclen/news_en/15mk/111600962/?ST=msbe |title=Many Plastic Parts Used for 'Thor/Roomy/Tank' Minivan |first=Takashi |last=Takada |work=Nikkei Technology Online |location=Japan |date=2016-11-16 |access-date=2017-04-15}}</ref> as the successor to the [[Daihatsu Coo|Coo]].<!-- The "Materia" nameplate was only used in Europe --> It sits below the [[Toyota Sienta|Sienta]] in Toyota's minivan line-up.

The Thor is currently sold only in Japan. It is not a [[kei car]], as the exterior dimensions and the engine displacement of 996&nbsp;cc exceed the [[Vehicle size class#Japan|class regulations]], but the small engine still incurs a modest annual [[Road tax#Japan|road tax]] obligation. From 2016 until 2020, the Tank was exclusive to ''[[Toyopet Store]]'' and ''[[Netz Store]]'', while the Roomy was once exclusive to ''[[Toyota Store]]'' and ''[[Toyota Corolla Store|Corolla Store]]''.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://blog.ihs.com/toyota-launches-all-new-minivan-model-in-japan,-also-sold-under-daihatsu-and-subaru-brands |title=Toyota launches all-new minivan model in Japan, also sold under Daihatsu and Subaru brands |work=IHS Markit Automotive Blog |date=2016-11-09 |access-date=2017-04-15}}</ref>

For the pre-facelift models, the regular Thor shared its front bumper shape with the Tank (both regular and Custom models) and the Justy Custom (with a redesigned upper grille and cross-hatched lower grille). The Thor Custom's bumper shape is shared with the Roomy (both regular and Custom models) and the regular Justy (with black grille slats instead of chrome). The Roomy uses standard taillights, while the Tank uses clear lens lights, which are reserved for the Custom versions of Thor and Justy. All Custom versions also wear an additional front splitter and chrome rear bootlid trim.

==Facelift==
The Thor and Roomy received a [[Facelift (automotive)|facelift]] on 15 September 2020, along with the discontinuation of the Tank model due to the merger of several of the Japanese Toyota dealership chains.<ref>{{Cite press release | url=https://global.toyota/jp/newsroom/toyota/33670235.html | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20241203230717/https://global.toyota/jp/newsroom/toyota/33670235.html | archive-date = 2024-12-03 | date = 2020-09-15 | title=ルーミーをマイナーチェンジ | trans-title = Roomy gets minor change | language = ja | work = Toyota Global Newsroom }}</ref> It was followed by the facelifted Justy in 24 September (the Justy Custom model being discontinued).<ref>{{Cite press release|url=https://www.subaru.co.jp/press/news/2020_09_24_9025/| archiveurl = https://web.archive.org/web/20241201175719/https://www.subaru.co.jp/press/news/2020_09_24_9025/ | archivedate = 2024-12-01 | date = 2020-09-24 | title = Subaru 「ジャスティ」一部改良モデルを発売 | trans-title = Subaru releases partially improved "Justy" model | language = ja | publisher = Subaru Corporation }}</ref>

The facelifted regular Thor shared its front styling with the regular Roomy, while the Thor Custom is shared with the Roomy Custom and the Justy.

